  "answer_text": "Here is a summary of the latest news on **Ukraine** as of June 2026:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\uddfa\ud83c\udde6 Ukraine \u2014 Latest News (June 2026)\n\n### \u2694\ufe0f Battlefield Situation\n\n- Ukraine's ability to impede the flow of Russian supplies and personnel to the front lines has grown in recent days, from the southern regions of Zaporizhia and Kherson to the eastern front, forcing the Russian army to a standstill, according to battlefield analysis.\n\n- Meanwhile, Ukraine has continued to strike refineries and munitions factories deep inside Russia, weakening its war effort.\n\n- General Oleksandr Komarenko stated that Ukrainian forces restored control over 285.6 km\u00b2 in the Oleksandrivka direction. In total, Ukrainian forces cleared 400 km\u00b2 of territory since the beginning of counteroffensive operations, and February 2026 became the first month since 2024 when Ukraine regained more territory than it lost.\n\n### \ud83d\ude80 Missile & Drone Attacks\n\n- On June 2, Russia fired a combination of 656 drones and 73 missiles into Ukrainian civilian areas, killing 23 people and injuring at least 130. Ukraine intercepted 91.7% of the drones and 90.6% of the cruise missiles, but only 27% of the ballistic missiles.\n\n- Russia produces 120 ballistic missiles a month, Zelenskyy told the Ukraine-NATO Council \u2014 twice as many as the Patriot interceptors the United States produces.\n\n### \ud83c\udfaf Ukrainian Long-Range Strikes\n\n- On May 31, Ukraine's 3rd Army Corps declared it had established fire control over the cities of Luhansk, Starobilsk, Alchevsk, Bryanka, and Kadiivka \u2014 all 50 to 90 km inside occupied Luhansk \u2014 marking the first time Ukraine declared such interdiction power over the eastern region.\n\n- Ukrainian forces also struck the city of St. Petersburg as Russian President Vladimir Putin arrived there for a high-profile economic forum, and President Zelenskyy wrote him an open letter telling him he could not win the war.\n\n### \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f Political Changes\n\n- Kyrylo Budanov, head of military intelligence (HUR), was appointed to replace Andriy Yermak as head of the Office of the President of Ukraine.\n\n- President Zelenskyy dismissed Lieutenant General Serhii Deineko as head of the State Border Guard Service of Ukraine, and Vasyl Malyuk was also forced to resign as head of the SBU.\n\n---\n\nWould you like more details on any specific aspect of the situation in Ukraine? \ud83c\udf0d",
